[15:25:30Z] FILES:    ls [-l] [dir], cd [dir], pwd, cat <path>
[15:25:30Z] PAGING:   head <path> [n], tail <path> [n]  (first / last n lines, default 10)
[15:25:30Z] TEXT:     grep [-i] [-n] [-v] [-c] <pattern> <path>  (fixed string; ^ and $ anchor)
[15:25:30Z]           wc [-l|-w|-c] <path>  (lines, words, bytes)
[15:25:30Z] WRITE:    touch <path>, write <path> <text>, append <path> <text>, rm [-r] [-f] <path>
[15:25:30Z] DIRS:     mkdir <path>, rmdir <path>  (create / remove empty directories)
[15:25:30Z] MOUNT:    mount write|append|rm|mkdir <path> [text]  (the one namespace, by prefix)
[15:25:30Z]           rm -r <dir>  (recursively delete a directory tree; root refused)
[15:25:30Z] COPY:     cp [-f] <src> <dst>  (copy a file; cp FILE DIR/ lands as DIR/<leaf>)
[15:25:30Z]           cp -r <srcdir> <dst>  (recursively copy a directory tree)
[15:25:30Z] MOVE:     mv [-f] <src...> <dst>  (move/rename a file or dir, O(1); mv SRC DIR/ lands as DIR/<leaf>)
[15:25:30Z] FLAGS:    default is no-clobber; -f = force overwrite (rm: quiet on missing), -n = no-clobber
[15:25:30Z] WILDCARD: * / ? in the last path component - ls/cat/rm/cp/mv expand it (e.g. rm *.TMP, cp *.TXT DOCS/)
[15:25:30Z]           (create/edit/delete/copy/move files & dirs anywhere in the tree; sync = write-through, durable)
[15:25:30Z] TREE:     find [root] <pattern>  (recursive glob search), du [dir]  (recursive size tally)
[15:25:30Z]           uptime  (seconds since boot; shows the wall clock when set)
[15:25:30Z] INSPECT:  stat <path>  (full on-disk detail), hexdump <path> [off] [len]  (bounded)
[15:25:30Z] NATIVE:   the plain file verbs reach the native volume: `/` native, /boot the boot FAT, /usb stick
[15:25:30Z]           setfattr <path> <key>=<value>, setfattr -x <key> <path>  (typed attributes: 42 1.5 "s" b64:.. [f,f])
[15:25:30Z]           getfattr <path> [key]  (one or all attributes), query <expr>  (id path of every match)
[15:25:30Z] SNAP:     snap list, snap create <name>, snap drop <gen>  (retained roots / snapshots)
[15:25:30Z]           snap ls <gen> [path], snap cat <gen> <path>  (read a snapshot; current-ACL enforced)
[15:25:30Z] CLOCK:    date, date -s YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM[:SS]  (seeds mtime stamps; unset = honest dashes)
[15:25:30Z]           time  (shared civil clock: ISO-8601 UTC + source; unsynced until SNTP/date -s)
[15:25:30Z] SMP:      ps (per-CPU run queues)
[15:25:30Z]           <name>      (just type it: lumen opens its window and the prompt returns; net runs, then prints its exit)
